<title>HUNGARY: Hungary two-mth govt bond yield rises to 18.79 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary two-mth govt bond yield rises to 18.79 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Hungary's two-year government bonds was set at 18.79 percent, up from 18.48 percent at an auction held one month ago, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    23 June 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    24 July 1999</p>
<p>    Total on offer			15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received		 31,485 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated		     15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued			  19,500 million forintd</p>
<p>    Average annual yield		18.79 pct</p>
<p>    Average price			 97.52 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price			 97.90 pct</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
